  <section id="free-launch">
    <h2>Where is a Free River Kayak Launch?</h2>
    <p>
      Finding a free river kayak launch can save you significant money over a season. While marinas and private boatyards often charge a fee (ranging from £5 to £15), you can frequently find free access at:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Local authority parks that border rivers.</li>
      <li>Environment Agency managed slipways (provided you have your waterways license).</li>
      <li>Public road bridges where rights of way cross the water.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="best-rivers">
    <h2>Discovering the Best Rivers for Kayaking UK</h2>
    <p>
      What makes a river great depends entirely on your skill level. The best rivers for kayaking uk range from the gentle meanders of the River Thames to the thrilling rapids of the River Wye or the Dee.
    </p>
    <p>
      In our experience organizing data for the UK Rivers directory, we highly recommend beginners start on slow-moving, non-tidal stretches. These sections offer predictable currents and easy navigation, allowing you to focus on your paddle strokes rather than fighting the water.
    </p>
